===== api diff =====
Sends one read-only request to two configured envs ([env.<name>] in
the api config) and prints a structural diff, with jq-style paths. Each env
uses its own token (token_env, or the shell session's token for the env you are
logged in to): one env's token is never sent to the other.

Only GET and GraphQL queries are supported. Mutations and subscriptions are
refused, because diff would run them against both envs.

Exit status: 0 identical, 1 different (like diff(1)), other codes for errors.

Usage:
  api diff --envs a,b <path> [.filter]   |   diff --envs a,b --gql [-e endpoint] <query> [-V k=v] [.filter] [flags]

Examples:
  api diff --envs dev,thien /rest/v2/smart-content/<id> .data
  api diff --envs dev,thien /rest/v2/smart-content '.data | length'
  api diff --envs dev,thien --ignore .data.updatedAt --ignore .meta /rest/v2/x
  api diff --envs dev,thien --gql -e v2/user 'query { me { id name } }' .data

Flags:
      --array-key string           match array elements by this field (e.g. id) instead of by position: a reordered list is not a difference
      --columns strings            with --table: the columns to show, in order (a,b,c)
  -c, --compact                    compact JSON output
      --connect-timeout duration   connect time limit (env CURL_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, seconds) (default 10s)
      --dry                        print the curl command instead of sending
  -e, --endpoint string            (--gql) path appended to the GraphQL base, or a full URL
      --envs api config show       the two envs to compare, e.g. dev,thien (from api config show)
      --gql                        compare a GraphQL query instead of a GET
      --har string                 also write the exchange to a HAR file (appends; secrets are masked)
      --har-secrets                with --har: keep tokens, cookies and passwords in the file (dangerous to share)
  -H, --header stringArray         extra header, "Name: value" (repeatable)
      --ignore stringArray         ignore a path and everything below it (repeatable), e.g. .data.updatedAt
  -i, --include                    print the status line and response headers
  -k, --insecure                   skip TLS certificate verification
      --json                       print the result as JSON (same exit status)
      --no-auth                    do not send the bearer token
  -o, --output string              write the body to a file
  -Q, --query stringArray          query parameter key=value (repeatable)
  -R, --raw-body                   print the body untouched: no filter, no pretty-print
  -r, --raw-output                 print string results without quotes (jq -r)
      --retry int                  retry transport errors and 502/503/504 N times
      --summary                    print a status/type/time/size footer to stderr (env API_SUMMARY)
  -t, --table                      print an array of objects (or one object) as a table
      --timeout duration           total time limit (env CURL_MAX_TIME, seconds) (default 5m0s)
      --trust-hosts                send your token to an absolute URL on another host (default: only to the active base URL)
  -V, --var stringArray            (--gql) variable key=value or key:=json (repeatable)
  -v, --verbose                    print request and response headers to stderr

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

===== api doctor =====
Runs a set of offline checks and prints one line each. Exit 1 if anything
fails; warnings alone exit 0. --online also tries the active base URL.

Usage:
  api doctor [flags]

Flags:
      --fix      chmod 600 the .env files that other users can read
      --json     print the checks as JSON (same exit code)
      --online   also GET the active base URL (5s limit)

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

===== api env =====
Show, load or clear the API session (API_BASE_URL, API_TOKEN, ...)

Usage:
  api env [command]

Available Commands:
  clear       Unset API_BASE_URL, API_GRAPHQL_URL, API_TOKEN and API_ENV
  example     Generate .env.example from your .env files, or check them for drift
  init        Create .env.<suffix> from .env.example (mode 0600)
  list        List the .env.<suffix> files in the project root
  load        Load .env / .env.<suffix> from the project root into the shell
  root        Print the project root (nearest directory with a .env or .git)
  status      Show env, base URL and token prefix
  use         Switch the shell to a configured [env.<name>] (base URL, GraphQL URL, token_env); no name = pick with fzf

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

Use "api env [command] --help" for more information about a command.

