===== api env example =====
Reads the KEY NAMES of .env and .env.<suffix> in the project root and prints a
.env.example. Values are blank. --keep-values keeps harmless ones, but keys that
look secret (TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, KEY, ...) and URLs with embedded
credentials are always blank. Nothing is written unless you pass --write.

--check compares every .env file with .env.example and lists, per file, the keys
it is missing and the keys the example does not document. It exits 1 on drift.

Usage:
  api env example [flags]

Flags:
      --check         report drift between .env.* files and .env.example (exit 1)
      --force         with --write: overwrite a different existing .env.example
      --keep-values   keep harmless values (secret-looking keys and credential URLs stay blank)
      --write         write .env.example instead of printing it

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

