===== api env load =====
Finds the nearest directory with a .env or .git and loads .env (or
.env.<suffix>) with allexport, so $VAR expansion inside the file works.

The file is sourced by the shell itself, not parsed here, which keeps zsh
semantics. --emit prints the statements for the shell to eval; the zsh "api"
function does that for you.

Usage:
  api env load [suffix] [flags]

Flags:
      --emit   print shell statements for eval

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
