===== api run =====
Runs a request from a .http file. <name> is looked up in .api/requests/ of the
project (name.http), or give a path. Pick a request by name or number; a file with
one request needs no selector. Variables: @var = value in the file, {{var}},
--var k=v, {{base}} {{graphql}} {{token}} {{env}} from the session,
{{$env API_NAME}} (API_* variables only), {{$uuid}}, {{$timestamp}}.

Safety: a .http file can come from a repository, so {{token}} and the session
bearer token are NOT sent to a host other than the active base URL, and a
request that would send {{token}} / {{$env ...}} there is refused, unless you
pass --trust-hosts.

Usage:
  api run [file|name] [request] [.filter] [flags]

Examples:
  api run --list                    # saved files in .api/requests
  api run users --list              # requests in users.http
  api run users "List users"
  api run users 2 .data.id --var id=42
  api run users --all --dry

Flags:
      --all                        run every request in the file, in order (stops at the first failure)
      --columns strings            with --table: the columns to show, in order (a,b,c)
  -c, --compact                    compact JSON output
      --connect-timeout duration   connect time limit (env CURL_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, seconds) (default 10s)
      --dry                        print the curl command instead of sending
      --har string                 also write the exchange to a HAR file (appends; secrets are masked)
      --har-secrets                with --har: keep tokens, cookies and passwords in the file (dangerous to share)
  -H, --header stringArray         extra header, "Name: value" (repeatable)
  -i, --include                    print the status line and response headers
  -k, --insecure                   skip TLS certificate verification
      --keep-going                 with --all: continue after a failure
      --list                       list saved files, or the requests inside a file
      --no-auth                    do not send the bearer token
  -o, --output string              write the body to a file
  -Q, --query stringArray          query parameter key=value (repeatable)
  -R, --raw-body                   print the body untouched: no filter, no pretty-print
  -r, --raw-output                 print string results without quotes (jq -r)
      --retry int                  retry transport errors and 502/503/504 N times
      --summary                    print a status/type/time/size footer to stderr (env API_SUMMARY)
  -t, --table                      print an array of objects (or one object) as a table
      --timeout duration           total time limit (env CURL_MAX_TIME, seconds) (default 5m0s)
      --trust-hosts                send your token to an absolute URL on another host (default: only to the active base URL)
      --var stringArray            set a {{variable}}: key=value (repeatable; beats @var in the file)
  -v, --verbose                    print request and response headers to stderr

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

===== api schema =====
With no subcommand it is a browser: pick an endpoint (from your config's
endpoints), then browse its queries, mutations and types in fzf with a live
preview. Enter prints the item; ctrl-e (or --edit) opens it in your editor
($API_EDITOR, $VISUAL, $EDITOR, or defaults.editor in the global config; nvim
when none is set).

Introspection helpers. <endpoint> is appended to the GraphQL base like
"api gql -e"; with --prefix v2/ a bare name such as "user" means v2/user.

  api schema names user --prefix v2/        # query and mutation names
  api schema type user Query --prefix v2/   # fields (with args), input fields or enum values
  api schema dump user --prefix v2/         # the whole introspection result
  api schema sync --prefix v2/ user auth    # cache schemas for fzf / television (~/.cache/ugql)

Usage:
  api schema [endpoint] [flags]
  api schema [command]

Available Commands:
  dump        Print the whole introspection result (the __schema object)
  endpoints   List the endpoints configured for the env (endpoints = [...])
  names       List the query and mutation names of an endpoint
  sync        Fetch every service's schema into the local cache the fzf / tv browsers read
  type        Show the fields (with args), input fields or enum values of a type
  types       List the type names of an endpoint, root query/mutation types first

Flags:
      --connect-timeout duration   connect time limit (env CURL_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, seconds) (default 10s)
      --dry                        print the curl command instead of sending
      --edit                       open the picked item in your editor instead of printing it
  -H, --header stringArray         extra header, "Name: value" (repeatable)
  -k, --insecure                   skip TLS certificate verification
      --no-auth                    do not send the bearer token
      --prefix string              prepended to a bare endpoint name (e.g. "v2/")
  -Q, --query stringArray          query parameter key=value (repeatable)
      --retry int                  retry transport errors and 502/503/504 N times
      --timeout duration           total time limit (env CURL_MAX_TIME, seconds) (default 5m0s)
      --trust-hosts                send your token to an absolute URL on another host (default: only to the active base URL)

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

Use "api schema [command] --help" for more information about a command.

