===== api secret =====
Secrets live in the operating system's credential store, never in a file this
tool writes. Refer to one anywhere a value is accepted as @keychain:NAME:

  api secret set upscale-dev --for https://api.dev.upscale.technology
  api login --gql ... -V input.password=@keychain:upscale-dev

--for binds the secret to the server(s) it may be sent to, like a browser's
password manager: a repo's config, an alias or a pasted command cannot make it go
anywhere else. A project config may only use bound secrets.

Entries are namespaced (the Keychain service is "api:NAME"), so this tool cannot
read or overwrite another application's items.

Usage:
  api secret [command]

Available Commands:
  bind        Add servers an existing secret may be sent to (the value is not re-entered)
  list        List the secrets you stored (names and where they may go; never values)
  rm          Delete a stored secret
  set         Store a secret (hidden prompt, or one line from stdin with --stdin)
  show        Check that a secret exists and where it may go (its value is printed only with --reveal)

Global Flags:
      --base string         base URL (default $API_BASE_URL)
      --color string        colour output: auto, always or never (env API_COLOR, NO_COLOR, JQ_COLORS) (default "auto")
  -C, --color-output        always colour the output (jq -C)
      --debug               print the equivalent curl command to stderr (or set API_DEBUG=1)
      --env string          use the [env.<name>] profile from config (see: api config show)
  -M, --monochrome-output   never colour the output (jq -M)
      --no-pager            never page long output (env API_PAGER sets the pager, empty disables)
      --token string        bearer token (default $API_TOKEN)

Use "api secret [command] --help" for more information about a command.

